Michael you and I got to check out  battle mode and doom eternal which is  actually pretty cool at least from what  we saw we played I don't know we played  a couple hours of it we checked out two  different maps and got to play all the  demons but what's the gist of it  gist of it is that it's a asymmetrical  multiplayer mode where one player is  doom Slayer with all the weapons and  abilities that you get from a single  player and a team of two on the other  side who can play as the demons and the  demons kind of play as different classes  because they have different abilities  they have different attacks ways of  moving around the map and I think it's  it has a lot more depth than I think  what you might see through in the  gameplay because once you get hands-on  with it you realize just how much is  going on  with battle mode and to talk about what  Doom Slayer brings for battle mode is  that it essentially has a recreation of  what the single-player is like because  you're using all those same abilities  because the demon team is spawning in  minions that are demons so you're going  through the same motions which is very  exciting because that is the best part  of the single-player game is getting in  those combat arenas using your chainsaw  using glory kills using the flame belt  you get armor back and all those things  to keep yourself alive as these two  demons are pounding you so it yeah the  way it's software has translated the  best parts of the single-player game  into the multiplayer if you play as Doom  Slayer it is it's impressive I think it  is so then what is the objective of  these rounds so is it just for the doom  Slayer to basically clear the map or do  you have to you have to kill the other  players yes good question so when if  you're playing as Doom Slayer you have  to kill the two player controlled demons  within a certain time frame though  because they respawn after like what was  it 30 seconds so some think it's about  20 seconds ish and you kind of have to  think about your the way you attack the  player control demons because if you  kill one  you put yourself on a sort of countdown  I need to get to the next demon before  the other one can respawn so it kind of  pushes you to be aggressive constantly  and what's the other demon spawns back  in they'll have like half health about  so it'll make it a little bit easier for  doom slayer it's not like you reset back  back to square one if you can't get to  the other demon in time but it still  puts a lot of pressure on you and that's  how you win rounds as doom Slayer  as demons you just need a kill doom  Slayer period and that sounds simple but  it's actually kind of complicated  because of how do player can keep  themselves alive with glory kills and  chainsaw kills so you might think that  you have dupe Slayer corner like you  know we're gonna win the round because  he's down to the 10th help this has  happened to me as doom Slayer I was down  to ten health I hit a chainsaw kill on  one of the minions got my ammo back got  armor and health back and then I came  back to win the round because then I  just turned it around it's like a game  of tug-of-war  but these rounds can go on for a very  long time they can very quickly there's  no time limit because at least what the  developers are saying is they really  like that back and forth that tug him  pulled between the doom Slayer and  demons and they were saying that people  in the office they would those games  would last 10 20 minutes or so if you've  got a really good doom Slayer and two  demons that are super well coordinated  speaking of demons though what were some  of the demons you got to play wow you  have we had five different demons that  we could get hands on with during the  demo time and there will be more in the  future but for now we have hands-on with  the man Kubis which is kind of a  slow-moving tank if you've seen him in  the single-player load that it has to  funk and throwers yeah yeah very like  just a tank that can take on a lot of  damage but also do a lot of damage  of course you're limited in terms of  mobility you also play as a CAC a demon  and fly across the map and it feels kind  of good to be able to have that freedom  to fly around on the map it's also  creates a different kind of strategic  aspect because in one of the maps when I  was on when I was playing doom Slayer  the CagA demon would fly as high as  possible and just like try and pick me  off and distract me while the other  demons  would come and attack me so I really  have to think about what all these  demons bring to the table because you  can coordinate in that fashion and my  favorite was the Marauder because you  can throw an axe on one hand and you  have a double-barrel shotgun on the  other so it's a really good aggressive  style of demon and I think that plays  closest to how dudes doom Slayer is so  you can do some really tricky things and  there's also revenant which has I think  like rocket launchers and stuff and some  other abilities some cool movement and  like jetpack so you can move around the  map more cleverly yeah there's there's  just a lot going on with the different  demons so we get a lot of time with  battle mode though and I think one of  the concerns especially if you're a  newer player or if you haven't played  through the single-player  I think balance might be all over the  place I mean especially like if you  haven't finished the single-player you  don't know what half these guns do and  you're going up against demons they  could crush you pretty quickly or the  opposite if you're fighting against  demons who just started and you're a  pretty good doom Slayer like you're  gonna know exactly which weapons you  need for each situation and you could  potentially clear them out pretty  quickly yeah I do have a bit of  hesitation when it comes to how  matchmaking is gonna play out because if  you if you're playing demons and you  have another player who isn't really  coordinating with you it can I could see  it falling apart rather quickly so you'd  want to have players on both sides who  kind of know what they're doing and  that's gonna be hard to find I'm sure  that the game will eventually find its  footing after release but I can see the  ways in which balance would be an issue  now talking to Marty strand Google  Martin internally they've had a lot of  testing with balance and all that stuff  but because they're putting a lot of  resources into this and they've gotten  to a point where internally there are  about 50/50 with that but of course  things shake out differently when it  actually goes public and people start to  dip their toes into the multiplayer mode  and I think you know we'll see updates  and tweaks to how that's going to work  but in terms of playing at a high level  it's a very exciting kind of take on it  whether you would like it or not it's  nice to see that do  internals trying something drastically  different from the standard multiplayer  modes that we saw into 2016 yeah I mean  I think that's one of the most exciting  things right is that at least they're  not trying that doom 2016 multiplayer  they're trying something different  hopefully it works out but only time  will tell  doom eternal comes out March 20th and  for more stay tuned the game spot  [Music]

